1
00:01:33,359 --> 00:01:33,680
Okay,

2
00:01:33,680 --> 00:01:34,680
that's it

3
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:35,879
for today's class.

4
00:01:35,879 --> 00:01:36,959
Everyone, go prepare well.

5
00:01:36,959 --> 00:01:37,599
Okay?

6
00:01:37,599 --> 00:01:39,079
Okay.

7
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:02,840
Senior Gu Chenyang.

8
00:02:04,319 --> 00:02:05,280
Chen Song.

9
00:02:11,439 --> 00:02:13,960
Interstellar Slam Dunk: Heart of the Machine.

10
00:02:14,479 --> 00:02:15,919
This is my new script.

11
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,800
You're the second reader.

12
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:18,879
The first one is Li Haoyu.

13
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:20,439
Yeah.

14
00:02:20,439 --> 00:02:21,719
He said I could

15
00:02:21,719 --> 00:02:22,960
show it to you.

16
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:26,520
What's this?

17
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:27,360
A sci-fi movie?

18
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:28,879
Not only a sci-fi movie,

19
00:02:28,879 --> 00:02:30,319
but also a sports drama.

20
00:02:30,599 --> 00:02:32,240
It's about a team of

21
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:34,000
abandoned robots

22
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,560
in the future.

23
00:02:35,879 --> 00:02:36,960
The inspiration for this story

24
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:39,319
comes from our Basketball Club.

25
00:02:39,639 --> 00:02:40,360
I even added

26
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:41,639
a role of a captain,

27
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:43,479
whose code name is Dubhe.

28
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:45,360
He is the brain of the team,

29
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:46,639
with a cool personality

30
00:02:46,639 --> 00:02:47,719
and meticulous planning.

31
00:02:48,039 --> 00:02:49,840
No matter how perilous the situation,

32
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:51,159
as long as he is there,

33
00:02:51,159 --> 00:02:52,680
it will be turned into safety

34
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:53,800
and lead to victory.

35
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:55,439
Senior Gu Chenyang,

36
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:56,520
this character

37
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:58,080
is based on you.

38
00:02:58,439 --> 00:03:00,080
At the last Arts Festival,

39
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,680
your quick thinking backstage

40
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:03,240
was just so cool.

41
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:04,680
I heard the basketball team

42
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:05,800
lost two games recently,

43
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,280
but I believe

44
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:11,199
as long as you're there,

45
00:03:11,199 --> 00:03:12,639
you will definitely turn the tide.

46
00:03:15,159 --> 00:03:15,840
Really?

47
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:16,840
Of course.

48
00:03:20,479 --> 00:03:21,280
Thank you.

49
00:03:24,199 --> 00:03:26,039
But I've only thought about

50
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:27,280
the character setting and details.

51
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:29,159
I haven't thought about how to write the script.

52
00:03:29,599 --> 00:03:30,879
Please give me some advice

53
00:03:30,879 --> 00:03:32,240
after you read it.

54
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:32,960
Okay.

55
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:34,680
I'll go now, senior.

56
00:04:14,599 --> 00:04:15,280
Coach

57
00:04:16,199 --> 00:04:16,920
I...

58
00:04:17,959 --> 00:04:19,399
I can still dribble with my left hand.

59
00:04:19,399 --> 00:04:21,079
I can play today.

60
00:04:21,079 --> 00:04:22,720
What tactic?

61
00:04:23,199 --> 00:04:23,720
Come here.

62
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:24,639
Sit down.

63
00:04:26,839 --> 00:04:29,199
You sitting down is the tactic.

64
00:04:30,279 --> 00:04:30,959
Coach

65
00:04:30,959 --> 00:04:32,600
I saw the tactic

66
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:33,439
you sent yesterday.

67
00:04:34,399 --> 00:04:36,079
It's a little bit complicated.

68
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:37,560
What's complicated?

69
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:38,800
I can explain it in detail.

70
00:04:39,079 --> 00:04:40,360
It's not your fault.

71
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:42,160
We don't have enough time.

72
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,560
There's only a week left before the game.

73
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:45,720
Changing tactics at the last minute is a big no-no.

74
00:04:45,959 --> 00:04:46,480
But I...

75
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:48,199
I know you're anxious.

76
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:49,839
But sometimes,

77
00:04:49,839 --> 00:04:51,920
it's better to do nothing than to do something wrong.

78
00:04:53,199 --> 00:04:53,800
Listen.

79
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:56,839
Come on.

80
00:04:56,839 --> 00:04:58,560
Check the notes for today.

81
00:05:01,199 --> 00:05:01,879
Li Haoyu.

82
00:05:01,879 --> 00:05:03,319
Li Haoyu can't control the ball.

83
00:05:03,319 --> 00:05:04,639
He's like playing with it every day.

84
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:05,720
Yes.

85
00:05:06,079 --> 00:05:06,920
Chenyang is right.

86
00:05:07,279 --> 00:05:07,800
And Lin Qingyuan.

87
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:09,600
Lin Qingyuan tends to lose focus on the field.

88
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:10,879
He missed several balls yesterday.

89
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:13,120
Yeah.

90
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:13,519
Well,

91
00:05:13,519 --> 00:05:14,839
I think so.

92
00:05:19,839 --> 00:05:20,720
Zhou Yang.

93
00:05:21,319 --> 00:05:22,079
Zhou Yang needs

94
00:05:22,079 --> 00:05:23,120
to be more active.

95
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:23,920
Only in this way

96
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:24,720
can he link us up.

97
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:27,160
Okay.

98
00:05:29,199 --> 00:05:30,000
Bin Yan.

99
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:30,920
I know.

100
00:05:40,759 --> 00:05:42,040
How long have you slept

101
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:43,480
since yesterday?

102
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:47,560
Just a heads-up,

103
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:50,439
the tactics you sent

104
00:05:50,439 --> 00:05:51,839
in the group at 3 AM.

105
00:05:56,199 --> 00:05:57,279
I know you have

106
00:05:57,279 --> 00:05:58,000
many reasons for turning me down.

107
00:05:59,319 --> 00:06:00,800
But your tense state

108
00:06:01,079 --> 00:06:02,399
might affect everyone.

109
00:06:06,079 --> 00:06:07,240
You should go rest first.

110
00:06:07,839 --> 00:06:08,959
It's better for everyone.

111
00:06:24,519 --> 00:06:25,360
Did you convince him?

112
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:26,800
Isn't it obvious?

113
00:06:30,319 --> 00:06:31,000
That's good.

114
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:55,519
Gu Chenyang,

115
00:06:55,879 --> 00:06:56,839
go back to training.

116
00:06:56,839 --> 00:06:58,079
Training what?

117
00:06:58,079 --> 00:06:59,680
How can I train when you're like this?

118
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,160
What's going on with you?

119
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:05,519
I just don't have confidence.

120
00:07:05,839 --> 00:07:06,879
The pressure is huge.

121
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:09,600
Will a plan give you confidence?

122
00:07:10,079 --> 00:07:11,800
Plans can't keep up with changes.

123
00:07:16,759 --> 00:07:17,600
Alright.

124
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:18,519
I have

125
00:07:18,519 --> 00:07:19,639
a very important plan.

126
00:07:19,639 --> 00:07:20,639
I must take you to carry it out.

127
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:22,160
What plan?

128
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:24,480
Super Invincible Lazy Fish Plan.

129
00:07:38,199 --> 00:07:39,199
Don't be so stiff.

130
00:07:39,199 --> 00:07:40,199
There's no surveillance here.

131
00:07:40,519 --> 00:07:41,920
Do you want to settle the matter

132
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:42,680
like we did when we were kids?

133
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:46,560
No need.

134
00:07:46,879 --> 00:07:47,759
I'm not in the mood.

135
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,399
Mood is something

136
00:07:50,399 --> 00:07:52,160
that comes with playing.

137
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:54,160
The way you are now

138
00:07:54,399 --> 00:07:55,319
is so similar to that day.

139
00:07:57,439 --> 00:07:58,160
Which day?

140
00:07:58,879 --> 00:08:00,160
The day we broke up.

141
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:11,800
You're amazing.

142
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:13,000
For the school charity,

143
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:13,759
each class

144
00:08:13,759 --> 00:08:15,279
has the teacher arrange the activity.

145
00:08:15,279 --> 00:08:16,319
But you applied for

146
00:08:16,319 --> 00:08:17,199
the charity sale.

147
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:18,959
I heard everyone praising you.

148
00:08:19,279 --> 00:08:20,360
Actually, it was my dad

149
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:21,279
who suggested it to me.

150
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:23,160
He said I'm already ten years old

151
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:24,519
and should try to independently plan

152
00:08:24,519 --> 00:08:25,680
and execute an event.

153
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,360
Only in the process of practice

154
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,839
can I grow up better.

155
00:08:29,079 --> 00:08:30,360
Is it necessary?

156
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:31,720
The purpose of the school

157
00:08:31,959 --> 00:08:33,000
is to

158
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,399
convey love happily.

159
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:37,080
Look.

160
00:08:37,799 --> 00:08:39,440
The Hand-holding Cat is finished.

161
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:40,240
Isn't it cute?

162
00:08:41,399 --> 00:08:42,279
So cute.

163
00:08:42,639 --> 00:08:43,559
This will be a hit

164
00:08:43,559 --> 00:08:45,000
at tomorrow's sale.

165
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:47,679
Right.

166
00:08:48,159 --> 00:08:49,919
My dad said we must

167
00:08:49,919 --> 00:08:50,840
check everything

168
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:51,960
one more time

169
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:53,120
before the sale.

170
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:53,799
I gotta go.

171
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:55,960
What...

172
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:57,360
What's the rush?

173
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:58,559
What could go wrong?

174
00:08:58,840 --> 00:09:00,000
As long as the dolls are cute,

175
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:00,919
they'll sell well,

176
00:09:00,919 --> 00:09:02,559
and the event will be a success.

177
00:09:03,639 --> 00:09:05,480
Look how cute this doll is.

178
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:07,120
This is the soul of the fundraiser.

179
00:09:08,799 --> 00:09:09,639
That makes sense.

180
00:09:09,919 --> 00:09:11,039
Let's work harder

181
00:09:11,039 --> 00:09:11,879
and make more.

182
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,159
Let's put on the clothes first.

183
00:09:15,159 --> 00:09:15,720
Okay.

184
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:22,840
Hello, Mr. Li.

185
00:09:23,279 --> 00:09:24,879
Why haven't the students come?

186
00:09:25,279 --> 00:09:26,559
Wasn't the event canceled?

187
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:29,639
It wasn't canceled.

188
00:09:29,879 --> 00:09:30,759
But the venue is leaking.

189
00:09:30,759 --> 00:09:32,159
We've moved to a new place.

190
00:09:32,720 --> 00:09:34,360
We all thought it was canceled.

191
00:09:34,879 --> 00:09:36,200
Didn't you notify everyone?

192
00:09:36,919 --> 00:09:37,519
No,

193
00:09:37,519 --> 00:09:38,919
I didn't.

194
00:09:38,919 --> 00:09:40,559
Can the students still come?

195
00:09:40,919 --> 00:09:42,000
It's too late today.

196
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,000
They won't make it in time.

197
00:09:43,320 --> 00:09:44,279
Alright then.

198
00:09:50,679 --> 00:09:51,600
Aunt Zhang,

199
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:52,399
it's me,

200
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:53,440
Yang.

201
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:54,360
I've been looking for a while,

202
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:55,039
but I still can't find

203
00:09:55,039 --> 00:09:56,039
your place.

204
00:09:56,240 --> 00:09:57,919
I'm on a small path

205
00:09:57,919 --> 00:09:59,120
next to the original venue.

206
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:00,759
Never mind.

207
00:10:00,759 --> 00:10:02,080
I need to go grocery shopping.

208
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:02,799
Maybe next time.

209
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:04,240
You're leaving?

210
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:05,559
Alright then.

211
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:10,759
Hello, Aunt Sun.

212
00:10:12,159 --> 00:10:13,360
Hello, Uncle Li.

213
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:16,080
Hello, Uncle Zhao.

214
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:18,879
Hello, Uncle Wang.

215
00:10:18,879 --> 00:10:19,840
We've changed the venue.

216
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:21,159
Can you still come?

217
00:10:22,799 --> 00:10:23,960
It's okay.

218
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:42,600
Gu Chenyang,

219
00:10:43,159 --> 00:10:44,000
I'm back.

220
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:46,000
Look at these.

221
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:47,000
Are they enough?

222
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:52,279
This...

223
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:55,759
Only one was sold this afternoon.

224
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:57,759
It's okay.

225
00:10:57,759 --> 00:10:58,440
I'll shout.

226
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:00,360
Charity sale!

227
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:02,080
Show your love for the children in the mountains!

228
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:02,919
Stop shouting.

229
00:11:03,279 --> 00:11:04,279
It's over.

230
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:06,840
Well,

231
00:11:07,679 --> 00:11:08,679
I'll buy them all.

232
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,039
I brought my lucky money.

233
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:12,679
Don't be like this.

234
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:13,799
It's not your fault

235
00:11:13,799 --> 00:11:14,960
that the venue had a problem.

236
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:16,279
It's my fault.

237
00:11:16,639 --> 00:11:17,840
My dad told me

238
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:19,639
to confirm all the details in advance

239
00:11:19,639 --> 00:11:20,759
to ensure everything goes smoothly.

240
00:11:20,759 --> 00:11:21,799
I didn't listen to him

241
00:11:21,799 --> 00:11:22,720
and carry it out properly.

242
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:24,200
So you're blaming me?

243
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:25,200
Yesterday,

244
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:25,879
I was the one who dragged you away

245
00:11:25,879 --> 00:11:26,919
and didn't let you confirm everything.

246
00:11:27,919 --> 00:11:29,120
That's not what I meant.

247
00:11:30,159 --> 00:11:31,759
I'll just buy this box, and that's it.

248
00:11:36,279 --> 00:11:38,000
Can you just leave me alone?

249
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:39,200
This is my charity event.

250
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:40,879
I don't need you to meddle.

251
00:11:40,879 --> 00:11:41,879
I gave up surfing

252
00:11:41,879 --> 00:11:43,240
just to spend time with you.

253
00:11:43,240 --> 00:11:44,559
I didn't ask you to.

254
00:11:44,559 --> 00:11:45,200
Fine.

255
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:46,759
I was just bored.

256
00:12:19,159 --> 00:12:20,240
I picked up this cat

257
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:21,759
the next day.

258
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:26,799
I waited at your house

259
00:12:26,799 --> 00:12:28,279
all night, but you never came back.

260
00:12:29,559 --> 00:12:30,639
Then you just disappeared

261
00:12:30,639 --> 00:12:31,759
for the whole summer.

262
00:12:32,039 --> 00:12:33,039
When you came back,

263
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:34,840
you were like a different person.

264
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:38,240
I'm sorry.

265
00:12:39,159 --> 00:12:40,720
Actually, that day,

266
00:12:40,919 --> 00:12:42,279
I wasn't blaming you.

267
00:12:43,039 --> 00:12:44,360
I was blaming myself.

268
00:12:45,919 --> 00:12:47,000
My dad was right.

269
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:49,440
Losing control comes with a price.

270
00:12:50,799 --> 00:12:51,799
Students,

271
00:12:51,799 --> 00:12:52,639
teachers,

272
00:12:52,639 --> 00:12:53,440
parents,

273
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:55,440
so many people believed in me

274
00:12:55,799 --> 00:12:57,240
and were looking forward to that event.

275
00:12:58,240 --> 00:12:59,440
But I messed it up.

276
00:13:01,759 --> 00:13:03,159
That feeling,

277
00:13:03,159 --> 00:13:03,720
I really don't want

278
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:04,840
to go through it again.

279
00:13:16,399 --> 00:13:17,120
Gu Chenyang,

280
00:13:18,159 --> 00:13:19,440
I bring this up again

281
00:13:20,080 --> 00:13:21,440
isn't to hear your apology.

282
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:23,840
I just don't like the way you are now.

283
00:13:24,519 --> 00:13:25,720
You're always

284
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:26,919
pushing yourself too hard.

285
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:28,559
You pretend you're not tired,

286
00:13:28,799 --> 00:13:29,960
but I can see it.

287
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:32,799
So,

288
00:13:32,799 --> 00:13:34,399
you don't like the way I am now?

289
00:13:36,039 --> 00:13:37,120
Not exactly.

290
00:13:38,799 --> 00:13:39,840
Both the old you

291
00:13:40,159 --> 00:13:41,159
and the new you

292
00:13:41,519 --> 00:13:42,480
are both pretty cool.

293
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:45,080
But the point is what do you think?

294
00:13:45,799 --> 00:13:47,320
You are not just your dad's son.

295
00:13:47,679 --> 00:13:49,000
You are also yourself.

296
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:58,600
So you

297
00:13:58,919 --> 00:14:00,000
are not mad at me anymore?

298
00:14:01,919 --> 00:14:03,519
It was not me who broke up with you.

